USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Smibert P", "lastName": "Smibert", "firstName": "Peter", "initials": "P", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Technology Innovation Lab, New York Genome Center, New York, NY, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Satija R", "lastName": "Satija", "firstName": "Rahul", "initials": "R", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "New York Genome Center, New York, NY, USA; Center for Genomics and Systems Biology, New York University, New York, NY, USA. Electronic address: rsatija@nygenome.org."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-9455-7245"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-3044-0897"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-7693-8957"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics", "supporting_data", "related_data"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "7", "volume": "177", "journalIssueId": 2828334, "dateOfPublication": "2019 Jun", "monthOfPublication": 6, "yearOfPublication": 2019, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Cell", "title": "Cell", "essn": "1097-4172", "issn": "0092-8674", "nlmid": "0413066", "isoabbreviation": "Cell"}, "printPublicationDate": "2019-06-01"}, "pubYear": "2019", "pageInfo": "1888-1902.e21", "abstractText": "Single-cell transcriptomics has transformed our ability to characterize cell states, but deep biological understanding requires more than a taxonomic listing of clusters. As new methods arise to measure distinct cellular modalities, a key analytical challenge is to integrate these datasets to better understand cellular identity and function. Here, we develop a strategy to \"anchor\" diverse datasets together, enabling us to integrate single-cell measurements not only across scRNA-seq technologies, but also across different modalities. After demonstrating improvement over existing methods for integrating scRNA-seq data, we anchor scRNA-seq experiments with scATAC-seq to explore chromatin differences in closely related interneuron subsets and project protein expression measurements onto a bone marrow atlas to characterize lymphocyte populations. Lastly, we harmonize in situ gene expression and scRNA-seq datasets, allowing transcriptome-wide imputation of spatial gene expression patterns. Our work presents a strategy for the assembly of harmonized references and transfer of information across datasets.", "affiliation": "New York Genome Center, New York, NY, USA.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print-Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't", "research-article", "Research Support, U.S. Gov't, Non-P.H.S.", "Journal Article", "Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "NIH HHS", "acronym": "OD", "grantId": "OT2 OD026673", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NICHD NIH HHS", "acronym": "HD", "grantId": "R01 HD096770", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NHGRI NIH HHS", "acronym": "HG", "grantId": "R21 HG009748", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIH", "grantId": "1DP2HG009623- 01", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIH", "grantId": "1OT2OD026673-01", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIH", "grantId": "5R01MH071679-12", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NICHD NIH HHS", "acronym": "HD", "grantId": "F32 HD075541", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Chan Zuckerberg Awards", "grantId": "HCA2-A-1708-02755", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NSF", "grantId": "DGE1342536", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NHGRI NIH HHS", "acronym": "HG", "grantId": "DP2 HG009623", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIMH NIH HHS", "acronym": "MH", "grantId": "R01 MH071679", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Chan Zuckerberg Awards", "grantId": "HCA-A-1704-01895", "orderIn": 0}]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Humans"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Gene Expression Profiling"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Sequence Analysis, RNA"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Software"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "